flowchart TB
  accTitle: Incremental migration path
  accDescr: Each architecture level remains independently runnable. A measured problem motivates the next level, which first runs in shadow mode and must pass configured gates. Failure returns to the prior known-good bundle.

  L0["Level 0<br/>Flat and simple"] --> P1["Measure routing or context problem"]
  P1 --> S1["Shadow Level 1 compiler"]
  S1 --> G1{"Gates pass?"}
  G1 -- "Yes" --> L1["Level 1<br/>Static routers"]
  G1 -- "No" --> L0

  L1 --> P2["Measure overlap or catalog-change problem"]
  P2 --> S2["Shadow Level 2 retrieval"]
  S2 --> G2{"Gates pass?"}
  G2 -- "Yes" --> L2["Level 2<br/>Filtered retrieval"]
  G2 -- "No" --> L1

  L2 --> P3["Measure policy or lifecycle problem"]
  P3 --> S3["Shadow Level 3 controls"]
  S3 --> G3{"Gates pass?"}
  G3 -- "Yes" --> L3["Level 3<br/>Governed retrieval service"]
  G3 -- "No" --> L2

  L3 -. "restore prior bundle" .-> L2
  L2 -. "restore prior bundle" .-> L1
  L1 -. "restore prior bundle" .-> L0

  classDef level fill:#20808D,stroke:#187078,color:#FFFFFF;
  classDef measure fill:#78909C,stroke:#607D8B,color:#FFFFFF;
  classDef shadow fill:#E08A3C,stroke:#C47530,color:#13343B;
  classDef gate fill:#FFF3E0,stroke:#C47530,color:#13343B;

  class L0,L1,L2,L3 level;
  class P1,P2,P3 measure;
  class S1,S2,S3 shadow;
  class G1,G2,G3 gate;
